{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-nox-speciation-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `process-nox-speciation` RunSpec -- total NOx running exhaust and its three chained species, NO, NO2 and HONO -- computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It is the ninth RunSpec this chain reproduces and the FIRST WHOSE OUTPUT IS NOT A RECTANGLE.\n\nWHY THAT MATTERS, and it is the whole reason the model changed. Until J78 the output relation was declared as a product: `n_outputPolProcess` x `n_outputCohort` x counties x months x day types, every block the same width. This run emits 436 rows as 124 + 104 + 104 + 104. The 20 cohorts the species blocks drop against their parent are fuel type 9, model years 2001 to 2020 -- electricity, every one -- and `NONO2Ratio` carries fuel types 1, 2, 3 and 5 and no row for 9. So a chained block is the parent's cohorts INTERSECTED with the ratio table's coverage, which is a join and not a property of either relation, and 124 + 104 x 3 and 109 x 4 are the same 436. The two declared numbers are now ONE, `n_outputRate`, and `rateSurvivorCount` recomputes it.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES (§23).\n\n* THE OUTPUT RELATION IS RAGGED. No other RunSpec here is: every one of the other eight emits blocks of equal width, so all eight could not tell the product from the sum. run-tests.sh prints which of the two a run is.\n\n* THE CHAIN TABLE IS KEYED BY A MODEL-YEAR GROUP. `PM10EmissionRatio`, the only chain table before this one, is keyed by a min/max RANGE; `NONO2Ratio` is keyed by the `modelYearGroupID` that `pollutantprocessmodelyear` gives the SPECIES -- not the parent -- so the port needed `rt_modelYearGroupID` as a value and not just the presence test J18 and J19 already made.\n\n* A SPECIES IS ITS PARENT TIMES A NUMBER, AND THE PARENT IS THE WORK. The speciation is one multiply. Everything under it -- the `emissionRateByAge` arm, the criteria fuel ratio, the NOx humidity correction -- is `expand-criteria`'s, and this run reaching 9.485e-06 on all 436 cells is what says the parent was right for a reason and not by luck.\n\n436 rows, worst cell 9.485e-06. Reproduced in pandas from the default database BEFORE the port, against this run's own parent values, at the same figure.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "process-nox-speciation",
      "nox-speciation",
      "chained",
      "ragged"
    ]
  },
